## General Response 1: A self-evolving agent explores the world model

GAIA-validation can be viewed as a world model. Our paper proposes a solution to the question that how a naive but self-evolving agent can acquire new and generalizable skills by exploring the world model and accumulate the experience from interaction with the world. Also, our agent can learn the world very well in an autonomous way. In a parallel and similar world(GAIA-test), we prove that our agent with generalizable skills(reusable MCPs) can still perform well after learning from the original world model(GAIA-validation). In the same way, HLE can be also viewed as a world model composed of multiple domain-specific world models(Math, Bio, etc.) and also a general agent can be converted into a specialist agent for a specific distribution of tasks through Alita-G.



